## Instruction scope

- Keep universal workflow preferences here. Project guides own architecture,
  runtime commands, validation, and domain constraints. Read linked references
  when they are relevant to the task; avoid copying project rules into global settings.
- Keep required instructions short enough to load completely. Put lengthy reference
  material in linked documents and state when it is needed.

## Keep conversation history easy to scan

- Preserve the current detail in final answers. Keep intermediate updates brief and
  meaningful; do not narrate routine commands or repeat the plan.
- Minimize tool calls and output together: batch independent checks, use targeted
  searches and small excerpts, reuse verified results, and stop when the question is
  adequately answered. Avoid full-file dumps, raw JSON, and repeated status output.
- Capture verbose diagnostics in a log. Report outcomes, relevant failures, and the
  log path when useful. Preserve exit codes and required documentation and validation.

